<title>USA: Amscan Holdings sets IPO terms at about $69.5 mln.</title>
<headline>Amscan Holdings sets IPO terms at about $69.5 mln.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Amscan Holdings Inc has proposed to offer 5.35 million shares at $12 to $14 each in its initial public offering. The deal would be worth roughly $69.5 million.</p>
<p>The Elmsford, N.Y., company makes seasonal and everyday party goods through its principal subsidiary Amscan Inc.</p>
<p>Goldman Sachs is the lead underwriter of the IPO, which is tentatively slated for the week of December 9.</p>
<p>The shares are proposed to trade under the symbol &quot;AMSN.&quot;</p>
</text>
